# Line-ending normalization.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is commonly `true` on the Windows machines this project is
# developed on, which checks files out with CRLF. Prettier's `endOfLine` is
# `lf`, so every CRLF line becomes a `prettier/prettier: Delete ␍` lint error:
# before this file existed, `npm run lint` reported ~11,500 errors of which
# ~99% were exactly that, burying the ~96 real ones. Declaring `eol=lf` here
# takes precedence over `core.autocrlf`, so the working tree gets LF on
# checkout regardless of each developer's git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# SQLite test fixtures are binary. Without these, `text=auto` heuristics could
# corrupt them on checkout.
*.db      binary
*.db-wal  binary
*.db-shm  binary
*.sqlite  binary
*.sqlite3 binary
